loadarg 0 fk fv
basearg 1 e
loadarg 16 1 ro
emit 2333081633
loadarg 2 1 rn
emit or 3531603976 shl add c 10 5
emit 3556769793
end

note ca_scal: a scalar argument just read (rk/rv/rt) for parameter p: flags into a register; its type
note must be the parameter's; stored at fr[q..q+2]. om4 CA1 .. CA_PUT.
fn ca_scal p ulong q ulong to void
if eq get rk 0 4
put rv 0 matreg 4 get rv 0 get rt 0
put rk 0 1
put rt 0 1
end
if ne get rt 0 ulong get fn_pt p
fail 7
end
put fr q get rk 0
put fr add q 1 get rv 0
put fr add q 2 0
end

note ca_arr: an array argument i of function f, call frame cb: one array passed twice is error 19.
note om4 CA_ARR .. CA_PUT.
fn ca_arr f ulong i ulong cb ulong to void
arrarg f i
j = ulong 0
while lt j i
if eq get fr add add cb mul j 3 2 get rt 0
fail 19
end
j = add j 1
end
q = add cb mul i 3
put fr q get rk 0
put fr add q 1 get rv 0
put fr add q 2 get rt 0
end

note ca_end: all arguments read: save, the arguments into X0.., BL, restore. Frame cb: 3 per argument,
note then cb+18 the parameter count, cb+19 the pool slot before the arguments. om4 CA_DONE .. CA5.
fn ca_end f ulong dst ulong cb ulong to void
